Abstract Factory Pattern
The Abstract Factory Pattern is an extension of the Factory Method Pattern.

The Abstract Factory Pattern aims to encapsulate a group of individual factories with a common theme.
It provides a way to create families of related objects without specifying their concrete classes.


Example:

The client uses the FactoeyProducer class to create a VehicleFactory based on the type.
This factory can make a specific car or motorcycle. FactoryProducer has a static method called getFactory.
It returns one of these concrete factories (ToyotaFactory or HondaFactory) based on the keyword.
These concrete factories manufacture specialized cars and motorcycles.

